# Koumarin — local development environment variables.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored and must NEVER be committed.
# This file holds PLACEHOLDERS ONLY and is safe to commit.
#
# Where real values live:
#   - locally        → your password manager, then this file's copy at `.env`
#   - deployed       → AWS SSM Parameter Store / Secrets Manager, synced into Kubernetes
#                      by the External Secrets Operator. Never in a manifest, never in a chart.
#   - once projects exist → prefer `dotnet user-secrets` over `.env` for ASP.NET services;
#                      it stores outside the repo tree entirely, so it cannot be committed
#                      by accident.
#
# Naming uses .NET's double-underscore convention, so FOO__BAR binds to configuration
# section "Foo", key "Bar" with no extra wiring.

# ---- CasinoApiPro sandbox — used by the Integration service ONLY ----
# Per ADR 0006, no other service may hold these.
CASINOAPIPRO__BASEURL=https://api.casinoapipro.com/v1
CASINOAPIPRO__APIKEY=ck_test_replace_me
CASINOAPIPRO__APISECRET=cs_test_replace_me

# Shared secret used to verify the HMAC on inbound settlement callbacks.
# This is the one credential standing between the internet and the ledger.
CASINOAPIPRO__CALLBACKSECRET=replace_me

# ---- local infrastructure (docker compose) ----
# Local-only credentials. Deployed environments get theirs from SSM.
POSTGRES__CONNECTIONSTRING=Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=koumarin;Username=koumarin;Password=localdev
REDIS__CONNECTIONSTRING=localhost:6379
RABBITMQ__CONNECTIONSTRING=amqp://guest:guest@localhost:5672/

# ---- inbound tunnel (Wave 3+) ----
# A seamless wallet cannot be developed without a public inbound URL: CasinoApiPro must
# reach your machine to settle a bet. Set this to the tunnel hostname you configure in
# their dashboard as the wallet base URL.
KOUMARIN__PUBLICCALLBACKBASEURL=https://replace-me.trycloudflare.com
